      "writtenOn": "2024-11-15T17:37:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The convention is that absent of explicit flush, the consumer is allowed to buffer data indefinitely.  (This is similar to e.g. the standard C library `fprintf()`.)\n\nAs the comment states the logic is to wait until more data arrives (and check if we can fill a USB packet then), or until the producer explicitly calls `queue_flush()`.  Both these will be signalled via `usb_written()` being called, which will use `hook_call_deferred()` to schedule a call that ends back here.",
      "parentUuid": "24e2f6ad_bc74f37c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "1db1c18ed744e74b8b5609e3627274654a49ad65",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
