        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-15T23:35:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The next patch sets a timer interrupt. However, if `STM32_USART_CR2_RTOEN` is not enabled, this data is stuck until the producer fills a packet, so this also needs to be within the same `#ifdef STM32_USART_CR2_RTOEN`.\n\nNo.  If `STM32_USART_CR2_RTOEN` is not defined (or if it is defined, but this particular usb-stream interface is connected to something other than a UART), then `usb_written()` will never have been invoked with a parameter of zero, and hence the `USB_STREAM_TX_USES_FLUSH` bit will not be latched, meaning that any data bytes are pushed into an outgoing USB buffer without delay.",
      "parentUuid": "b69ef735_f18d63ec",
