      "writtenOn": "2024-11-15T16:58:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This comment is misleading, since producers can\u0027t declare they use `flush()`, they just use it. Meaning, either:\n\n1. The first \"packet\" will always be sent as single bytes until the producer triggers a `flush()` once they believe enough data has been \"buffered\" (quotes, because the first packet\u0027s data isn\u0027t being buffered).\n1. They issue a `flush()` during init to set the flag.\n    * I don\u0027t recommend this, since it\u0027s using hidden/undocumented behavior in this specific USB module. Rather, a \"set stream capabilities\"-type function should be exposed for producers to indicate they want to use the flush feature.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "1db1c18ed744e74b8b5609e3627274654a49ad65",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a8393d56_3f486ba0",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb-stream.h",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-15T17:37:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the previous patch, I added the below comment inside `queue_flush()`, setting up such that this `flush()` during init would not be undocumented or specific to the USB consumer.  Should I rather move that comment to the header file, on the declaration of `queue_flush()`?\n```\n\t * Some producers will not make use of queue_flush(), and care has to\n\t * be taken that a consumer does not wait infinitely for a flush\n\t * request that never comes.  To handle this, consumers must eagerly\n\t * process data until the first time they get a notification with zero\n\t * length, which serves as indication that the producer uses the flush\n\t * semantics.  Producers can make a call to queue_flush() as part of\n\t * their initialization, to avoid any actual data being eagerly\n\t * processed.\n```\n\nThat being said, I agree that the potential performance hit from initial characters not being buffered before the first flush is completely negligible.",
      "parentUuid": "3dfe077d_7fd602ff",
